<title>SWITZERLAND: Baloise cuts some markets, 190 Swiss jobs.</title>
<headline>Baloise cuts some markets, 190 Swiss jobs.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baloise Insurance Group said it would withdraw from Italy, France and Spain to concentrate on more profitable core markets and cut 190 Swiss jobs in the next two years.  </p>
<p>Baloise said it would concentrate on expanding its existing markets in Switzerland, Germany, Belgium, Luxembourg and Austria.</p>
<p>&quot;Baloise makes money in these markets, even in relation to its equity,&quot; chief executive Rolf Schaeuble told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;We will separate from our subsidiaries in Italy, France and Spain. Measured by profitibility, these three markets do not count among the attractive markets for us in the European Union,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
